# Swarm roles (locked by user)

| Actor | Role | Model |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **This Cursor agent** | **Review only** — split work, AC, merge-review, report. Does **not** implement product UI/features. | — |
| **agy** | **Coder** | `gemini-3.1-pro-high` (fallback `gemini-3.1-pro-low`) |
| **opencode** | **Coder / fixer** | DeepSeek V4 Max Free if listed; else `opencode/deepseek-v4-flash-free` |

## Workflow

1. User request → controller decomposes into **disjoint** briefs:
   - `.agents/briefs/<ID>-agy.md`
   - `.agents/briefs/<ID>-opencode.md`
2. Dispatch both in parallel (owned paths must not overlap).
3. When both finish → controller reviews diffs + build; report in Vietnamese.
4. Hotfixes from review → assign back to **agy** or **opencode** (not self-code).

## Dispatch

```bash
# agy (Gemini 3.1 Pro)
cd /root/Restly && agy --dangerously-skip-permissions \
  --model gemini-3.1-pro-high --print-timeout 30m \
  --print "Execute .agents/briefs/<ID>-agy.md …"

# opencode (DeepSeek)
cd /root/Restly && opencode run --auto --dir /root/Restly \
  -m opencode/deepseek-v4-flash-free \
  --title "<ID>" \
  "Execute .agents/briefs/<ID>-opencode.md …"
```

If user names `deepseek-v4-max-free` and `opencode models` shows it, use that slug instead.

## Never

- Cursor agent coding product changes while swarm is active
- Two coders on the same file set
- OpenCode/agy used as “reviewer” — review is Cursor’s job
